reign investment and stimulate job growth. **The Verdict** Is it fair to say apartheid is basically the cause of the poverty? **Yes, it is the primary, foundational cause.** The scale of the inequality and the spatial divide of the country are apartheid’s direct inheritance. However, a common analogy used in South Africa is this: **Apartheid gave the country a devastating, deep wound. But the post-1994 government has, in many ways, failed to apply the right medicine, and through corruption and mismanagement, has actively infected the wound.** Therefore, while apartheid created the poverty, modern governance failures are largely the reason why the country has stalled in its efforts to eradicate it.
